# The JZLA20 engine at the `∗`-regular closure, and the discharge of `DivLoc`

This file assembles the two halves of the subproject.

* `Work.ORDivLoc.starClosureDivOn_of_clDivOn` — the induction of [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] at the
  `∗`-regular closure: if the division closure `D_{K[H],V}` of the image of `K[H]` in
  `V = R(K[H], U(G))` is a division ring and the structure map `K[H] →+* V` is epic, then `V`
  itself is a division ring (`Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isDivisionRing_of_isDivisionRing_divisionClosure`).
* `Work.ORDivLoc.divLoc_of_clDivLoc` — **the deliverable**: node N6's output
  (`ClDivLoc K G φK`) and epicity of the structure maps imply `DivLoc K G φK`.
* `Work.ORDivLoc.clDivOn_of_hstep` — the raw form of node N6's output as delivered by
  `Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isUnit_of_mem_divisionClosure` (the induction, axiom-clean), from
  the existence of the induction environments `Work.ORHughesFree.Thm61Step`.

The only remaining input on the node N6 side is the *construction* of the induction environment
`Thm61Step K G U φ H` for every finitely generated non-trivial `H ≤ G` — i.e. precisely the
theorem `Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.thm61Step_nonempty`, whose analytic input is
[JZLA20, Proposition 3.11] (`Work.ORHughesFree.IsHughesFreeEnv`).  It is *not* used here (its file
is still a stub), it is taken as the explicit hypothesis `hstep`.  See `N6Criterion.lean` for the
conversion of the N5-vocabulary form of Proposition 3.11 into `IsHughesFreeEnv`.
-/
import Submission.Work.ORDivLoc.DivisionClosure
import Submission.Work.ORDivLoc.Vocabulary
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.Thm61Proof
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.HughesFreeEnv

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

universe u v

namespace Work.ORDivLoc

open Work.ORHughesFree

variable {G : Type v} [Group G] {K : Type u} [Field K]

/-! ## Nontriviality of the `∗`-regular closure -/

/-- The `∗`-regular closure of the image of `K[H]` in `U(G)` is nontrivial: it contains the image
of `1 : K[H]`, which is nonzero in the nontrivial ring `U(G)`. -/
instance nontrivial_starClosureOfSubgroup (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) :
    Nontrivial ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H) :=
  ⟨1, 0, fun h => by
    have h' : (1 : E.U) = 0 := by simpa using Subtype.ext_iff.mp h
    exact one_ne_zero h'⟩

/-- The division closure of the image of `K[H]` in `V` is nontrivial: it contains the image of
`1 : K[H]`, which is nonzero because `U(G)` is nontrivial. -/
theorem nontrivial_divisionClosure_cod (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) :
    Nontrivial ↥(divisionClosure (Set.range (starClosureCod E φK H))) :=
  ⟨1, 0, fun h => by
    have h1 : (1 : ↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H)) = 0 := by
      simpa using Subtype.ext_iff.mp h
    have h2 : (1 : E.U) = 0 := by simpa using Subtype.ext_iff.mp h1
    exact one_ne_zero h2⟩

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

section TypeZero
/-- **Node N6's output, at `Type`.**  From the existence of the induction environments
`Thm61Step K ↥H V φ H₀`, every nonzero element of the division closure of the image of `K[H]` in
`V` is a unit.

This is the axiom-clean induction of [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1]
(`Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isUnit_of_mem_divisionClosure`); note that it needs **no** epicity,
no rank function and no Hughes-freeness: those enter only through the construction of the
environments `Thm61Step`.

The statement is at `Type` because the engine's environment `Work.ORHughesFree.Thm61Step` is
(unlike everything else in this directory) not universe-polymorphic; see the module docstring. -/
theorem clDivOn_of_hstep {K : Type} [Field K] {G : Type} [Group G]
    {E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G} (φK : K →+* ℂ)
    [Algebra K E.U] {H : Subgroup G}
    (hstep : ∀ H₀ : Subgroup ↥H, H₀.FG → H₀ ≠ ⊥ →
      Nonempty (Thm61Step K ↥H (↥(starClosureOfSubgroup E φK H)) (starClosureCod E φK H) H₀)) :
    ClDivOn E φK H :=
  ⟨nontrivial_divisionClosure_cod E φK H,
    Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isUnit_of_mem_divisionClosure (starClosureCod E φK H) hstep⟩

/-! ## The last step of [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] at the `∗`-regular closure -/

/-- **Node N6's output implies that the `∗`-regular closure is a division ring**, provided the
structure map `K[H] →+* V` is epic (which holds because `V` *is* the `∗`-regular ring generated by
its image: this is `Work.ORDivLoc.isEpic_starClosureCod`).

This is the last step of [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1]: an epic homomorphism out of a division ring is
surjective, so if the division closure `D_{K[H],V}` of the image is a division ring, then
`V = D_{K[H],V}` is one
(`Work.ORHughesFree.isDivisionRing_of_isDivisionRing_divisionClosure`).

**This route is an alternative to `Work.ORDivLoc.divOn_of_clDivOn`**, which reaches `DivLoc`
directly and thereby avoids the epicity hypothesis altogether (and is universe-polymorphic).  It is
recorded because it produces the *directory's* `StarClosureDivOn`, i.e. the conclusion of the JZLA20
engine in the form in which `Work.ORHughesFree.Section6.isDivisionRing_of_full` states it.  Its
statement is at `Type` because `IsEpic` is a `Prop` about ring homomorphisms within one universe
and the two lemmas it invokes are stated at `Type`. -/
theorem starClosureDivOn_of_clDivOn {K : Type} [Field K] {G : Type} [Group G]
    {E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G}
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] {H : Subgroup G}
    (hφ : IsEpic (starClosureCod E φK H)) (h : ClDivOn E φK H) : StarClosureDivOn E φK H :=
  Work.ORHughesFree.isDivisionRing_of_isDivisionRing_divisionClosure
    (starClosureCod E φK H) hφ h

/-! ## The `∗`-compatibility of the structure map -/

/-- **The structure map `K[H] →+* V` into the `∗`-regular closure is `∗`-compatible** in the sense
of `Work.ORHughesFree.StarCompatible`: it carries the group-like unit `λ · h` to the image of
`h⁻¹`.  This is the conversion of the envelope's `ι_star` into the vocabulary of
[JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] (where only the group basis is mentioned), and it is one of the hypotheses
of the construction `thm61Step_nonempty` of the induction environment. -/
theorem starCompatible_starClosureCod {K : Type} [Field K] {G : Type} [Group G]
    (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G)
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) [Algebra K E.U] (H : Subgroup G) :
    StarCompatible (starClosureCod E φK H) := by
  have hstarℂ : ∀ g : G, star (E.ι (MonoidAlgebra.single g 1)) =
      E.ι (MonoidAlgebra.single g⁻¹ 1) := fun g => by
    rw [← E.ι_star]
    congr 1
    simp
  intro h
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  simp only [coe_star_starSubring, starClosureCod_apply, Work.ORBridgeLinnell.toUK_single,
    one_smul, Work.ORBridgeLinnell.genU_apply]
  exact hstarℂ (h : G)

end TypeZero

end Work.ORDivLoc
